# Local E2E suite against api.minimax.io.
#
# The bundled CLI's provider layer supports BOTH the OpenAI Responses
# protocol (`POST /v1/responses`) and the Anthropic Messages protocol
# (`POST /v1/messages`). MiniMax serves both at the same hostname:
#   - https://api.minimax.io/v1          → OpenAI Responses
#   - https://api.minimax.io/anthropic   → Anthropic Messages
#
# The cross-protocol dispatcher auto-detects from the URL path
# (`/anthropic/...` commits to Anthropic; otherwise OpenAI first,
# Anthropic fallback on 404 — PR #32).
#
# Per-row budgets (~26 calls total) are enforced by `makeCountingFetch`
# in `test/e2e/minimax-e2e-helpers.ts`; a regression that doubles calls
# fails the suite loudly instead of re-billing the upstream gateway.
# See README "End-to-end (e2e) tests" for the per-bucket inventory.
#
# To run locally:
#   1. Set UMACTUALLY_E2E_MINIMAX_KEY below (or in your env).
#   2. npm run test:e2e
#
# To skip the suite (default behavior when the key is absent), just
# run `npm test` — vitest's e2e project is excluded by default.

UMACTUALLY_E2E_MINIMAX_KEY=
